breech clout you aren't wearing (after which it may as well be 
called a towel).  A +5 towel does nothing special when a)pplied or
P)ut on.

	Classes that start without body armor get a long tunic in-
stead.  (10% breech clout for male healers & wizards; 20% for male 
monks & priests; eliminate the chance of an initial blindfold / 
towel for samurai, tourists, and wizards.)

	Monks can wear breech clouts and long tunics without the
usual body armor penalty.

	Shopkeepers refuse to admit nude males (no body armor and
no cloak) and nude or topless females (no body armor OR just a 
breech clout and no cloak).


